=== Probe: which Bockstein/Steenrod names are actually bound?
  SteenrodAlgebraOperations: NOT bound
  Sq: bound
  Sq1: NOT bound
  Bockstein: bound
  BocksteinHomomorphism: NOT bound
  Mod2SteenrodAlgebra: bound
  ModPSteenrodAlgebra: bound
  BocksteinHomology: bound
  HAP_bockstein: bound
  HAP_chain_bockstein: bound
  ModPRingGenerators: bound

=== Build mod-2 Steenrod algebra of D_8 up to degree 4
  A = Algebra( GF(2), [ v.1, v.2, v.3, v.4, v.5, v.6, v.7, v.8, v.9, v.10, 
  v.11, v.12, v.13, v.14, v.15, v.16, v.17, v.18, v.19, v.20, v.21 ] )
  ModPRingGenerators(A) = [ v.1, v.2, v.3, v.4 ]
  degrees                = [ 0, 1, 1, 2 ]

=== Sq^1 = Bockstein on degree-1 generators of H^*(D_8; F_2)
  degree-1 generators: [ v.2, v.3 ]
The Bockstein operation is not defined for this algebra.
    Sq^1(v.2) = fail
    Sq(A,1,v.2) = v.4+v.5
The Bockstein operation is not defined for this algebra.
    Sq^1(v.3) = fail
    Sq(A,1,v.3) = v.6

=== Cross-check on a degree-2 element (Sq^1 of a square)
  y = v.2^2 (degree 2)
The Bockstein operation is not defined for this algebra.
  Sq^1(y)  = fail
  Sq(A,1,y) = 0*v.1

=== Outcome
HAP exposes Sq^1 cleanly via Sq(A, 1, w) where
    A := Mod2SteenrodAlgebra(G, N).
Concretely on D_8 = SmallGroup(8,3) with generators v.2, v.3 in
degree 1 we get Sq^1(v.2) = v.4 + v.5 and Sq^1(v.3) = v.6,
and the Cartan relation Sq^1(v.2^2) = 2 v.2 Sq^1(v.2) = 0 mod 2
checks out.

Caveat: the higher-level wrapper Bockstein(A, w) prints
'The Bockstein operation is not defined for this algebra.'
and returns fail on Mod2SteenrodAlgebra output, even though
Sq(A, 1, w) works on the same A. This appears to be because
Mod2SteenrodAlgebra populates A!.squares[2] but on this code
path A!.bockstein is not bound (cf. steenrod.gi lines 215-216).
Workaround for downstream Tasks: prefer Sq(A, 1, w) over
Bockstein(A, w). Both are documented HAP entry points.

The plan's guessed names (SteenrodAlgebraOperations, ops.Sq1)
are NOT the HAP API.
